# Docker
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=homecoming-hackathon-2026

# Postgres Database
# Written out flat rather than with ${VAR} interpolation: expansion only works
# in tools that opt into it (Next.js, docker-compose, prisma.config.ts), so a
# plain `node --env-file` run would otherwise get a literal "${POSTGRES_USER}".
POSTGRES_USER=postgres
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres
POSTGRES_DB=postgres
# Host port 5433, not 5432, so this doesn't collide with another local Postgres.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5433/postgres?schema=public

# ── AI ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every AI call in the app is listed in lib/ai/tasks.ts and routed through
# lib/ai/provider.ts. `npm run ai:report` prints the inventory.

# Which backend serves those calls.
#   ollama     — a model on this machine. Free, slower, for tuning prompts.
#   anthropic  — Claude. Costs money. What the demo runs on.
# Defaults to anthropic when unset, so a deploy that forgets this still works.
AI_PROVIDER=ollama

# AI_PROVIDER=ollama only. Needs `ollama serve` running.
# `mistral` is the default because it's commonly already pulled; `qwen2.5:7b`
# follows instructions and fills JSON schemas noticeably better.
# Per-task override, beats AI_PROVIDER for that one call. Job ranking is slow
# locally (~2min for 20 listings) and ~$0.01 a click on Haiku, so this is the
# usual split: coaching free and local, ranking on the API.
# Quiz coaching is on the API too, and since it became a conversation the gap
# matters more than it did. Measured per turn:
#   mistral      ~33s, and it opens with "Hello there!" and reaches for
#                headings and bullet lists, which the coach prints literally
#   Haiku 4.5    1-3s, ~$0.0015, clean prose
# A student waiting half a minute for each follow-up stops asking them, which
# is the whole feature. Set this to ollama if you want it free and are willing
# to demo a tutor that answers at that pace.
AI_PROVIDER_QUIZ_COACHING=anthropic

# Skill extraction and resume reading are pinned to the API. Measured on mistral:
# 10-42s per listing, and it tagged one listing with 37 of the 46 skills --
# a row like that matches everyone and corrupts every later ranking. On Haiku
# it is ~1.5s and $0.004, charged once per listing ever, because the result is
# stored. Set this to ollama only if you are willing to re-check what it wrote.
AI_PROVIDER_JOB_SKILL_EXTRACTION=anthropic
AI_PROVIDER_RESUME_EXTRACTION=anthropic

OLLAMA_MODEL=mistral
OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434
# Local generation is slow. Raise this if a big model keeps timing out.
OLLAMA_TIMEOUT_MS=180000

# AI_PROVIDER=anthropic only. Without it, the AI features report the missing
# key instead of failing. Get one at https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Authentication (Better Auth)
# Signs the session cookie. Generate one with: openssl rand -base64 32
# Required in production; lib/auth/server.ts falls back to an insecure dev
# value locally so a fresh clone can run `npm run dev` straight away.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=""
BETTER_AUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# ── Public URL ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The address this app answers on, for links handed to other people:
# certificate share links, and the certUrl that lands on someone's LinkedIn
# profile. Leave it unset for local development — the app falls back to the
# browser's origin and the LinkedIn buttons explain that they need a real
# deployment. Set it when you deploy and they start working, no code change.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://your-app.vercel.app
